---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { book, href, chapterHref, groups, paths } from '../lib/book';
const contracts = [
  {id:'conditioning',name:'Conditioning',text:'Which information actually conditioned the decision? Context, retrieval, and memory must preserve the distinctions an action depends on.',chapter:17},
  {id:'authority',name:'Authority',text:'What is the system currently permitted to do? A plausible proposal, a retrieved instruction, and an executable grant are different objects.',chapter:29},
  {id:'effects',name:'Effects',text:'What happened outside the model? Durable operation identities and service evidence distinguish a committed action from an unresolved attempt.',chapter:32},
];
---
<Shell>
  <main id="main" class="site-width home-publication">
    <section class="publication-opening" id="top">
      <div class="opening-copy">
        <p class="edition-line">A technical monograph <span>29 October 2026</span></p>
        <h1>Context, memory,<br />and control.</h1>
        <p class="opening-subtitle">The architecture of adaptive AI systems.</p>
        <p class="publication-byline">By <a href={href('about/')+'#authorship'} rel="author" data-author-credit>{book.metadata.author}</a></p>
        <p class="opening-lede">An agent is more than a model. Its decisions depend on what it observes, what it remembers, what it can execute, and how its effects are verified.</p>
        <p class="opening-description"><em>Agentic State</em> connects these mechanisms across models, learning, sessions, memory, tools, protocols, orchestration, evaluation, security, and self-improvement.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={chapterHref(book.chapters[0].slug)}>Read the book <Icon name="right" size={17} /></a><a class="button secondary" href={href('book/')}>Explore the chapters</a><a class="quiet-link" href={href('downloads/agentic-state.pdf')}>PDF <Icon name="download" size={15} /></a></div>
        <p class="publication-record">34 chapters <span>·</span> 482 pages of main text <span>·</span> 356 references</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="opening-plate" aria-label="The organizing questions">
        <figure class="observatory-plate"><img src={href('brand/agentic-observatory-v2.png')} alt="Conceptual engraving of an information observatory, connecting an archive, a central decision instrument, and an execution gate." width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption><span>THE AGENTIC OBSERVATORY</span><span>Conceptual illustration</span></figcaption></figure>
        <div class="contract-explorer"><div class="contract-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Explore the three consistency contracts">{contracts.map((c,i)=><button role="tab" id={`contract-${c.id}`} data-contract={c.id} aria-selected={i===0?'true':'false'} aria-controls={`panel-${c.id}`}>{c.name}</button>)}</div>{contracts.map((c,i)=><div class="contract-panel" id={`panel-${c.id}`} role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby={`contract-${c.id}`} data-contract-panel={c.id} hidden={i!==0}><p>{c.text}</p><a href={chapterHref(book.chapters[c.chapter-1].slug)}>Follow this question <Icon name="right" size={15} /></a></div>)}</div>
      </aside>
    </section>
    <section class="publication-index" aria-labelledby="contents-heading">
      <header class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE STRUCTURE OF THE ARGUMENT</span><h2 id="contents-heading">From a model to a system.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={href('book/')}>Complete contents <Icon name="right" size={18} /></a></header>
      <div class="index-volumes">{groups.map((group,i)=><a class="index-volume" href={href('book/')+`#group-${group.range[0]}`}><span class="volume-number">0{i+1}</span><div><h3>{group.name}</h3><p>{group.subtitle}</p></div><span class="volume-range">Chapters {group.range[0]}–{group.range[1]}</span><Icon name="arrow" size={21} /></a>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section class="research-position"><span class="eyebrow">A CROSS-LAYER RESEARCH PERSPECTIVE</span><div><h2>What must remain consistent<br />as an agent changes?</h2><p>The book separates the information that conditions a proposal, the authority that permits an operation, and the evidence that establishes its effects. Preserving one does not establish the others.</p><p>Mathematical formulations, identifiable implementations, and explicit evidence limits make those distinctions testable.</p><a class="text-link" href={href('about/')}>Read the contribution and its limits <Icon name="right" size={17} /></a></div></section>
    <section class="path-section" aria-labelledby="paths-heading"><header class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">ENTER THROUGH A RESEARCH QUESTION</span><h2 id="paths-heading">Four ways to read.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={href('reading-paths/')}>All reading paths <Icon name="right" size={17} /></a></header><div class="path-grid">{paths.map(path=><article class="path-card"><h3>{path.title}</h3><p>{path.summary}</p><div class="path-steps">{path.chapters.map(n=><a href={chapterHref(book.chapters[n-1].slug)} title={book.chapters[n-1].title}>Chapter {n}</a>)}</div></article>)}</div></section>
  </main>
</Shell>
